#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Post-deploy smoke test: drive the LIVE site with a real browser, and
# exit with an error that names the broken check if it is broken
# (docs/deploy-confidence-plan.md item 6).
# This catches the class of bug no local test can: the code is fine
# but the deploy is not (env vars, asset serving, a stale build).
#
# Read-only by design — production is real ledger data. Without
# credentials it checks the public surface: the login page renders
# with no console errors, and the API answers. With SMOKE_EMAIL and
# SMOKE_PASSWORD set it also logs in and renders the calendar on a
# daylight-saving month (the November escape) and the meal page. With
# SMOKE_ADMIN_EMAIL and SMOKE_ADMIN_PASSWORD set it signs in to the
# admin site (admin.<host>) and opens the dashboard and the
# reconciliations list. Each login is tried once. When the site refuses
# one, the checks behind it are skipped, the rest still run, and the run
# ends with code 2 and the variables to check.
#
# Exit codes:
#   0  Every check passed.
#   1  A check failed: the site is broken. The smoke test also ends
#      with 1 when it could not run at all (no browser, say).
#   2  The site answered and refused a login: the smoke credentials
#      are wrong. Every check that could run passed, but the checks
#      behind that login did not run, so this is not a pass either.
#   Any other code: the smoke test could not run (127: no node).
# The callers treat every code but 0 and 2 as a broken site.
# tests/smoke/checks.js (EXIT) uses the same numbers.
#
# On production these are the owner's own resident and admin accounts:
# bin/deploy reads them from .env, and the Deploy and Rollback workflows
# from the GitHub secrets. Production never gets a smoke resident: that
# would be a fake person on the community's shared screen (decided
# 2026-09-21, #68). The staging rehearsal makes its own smoke resident,
# so the resident checks run there too. Staging has no admin site.
#
# It never prints a password (tests/smoke/checks.js, redact).
#
# Usage:
#   bin/smoke                        # against https://comeals.com
#   bin/smoke http://localhost:3000  # against any other base URL
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."

SMOKE_URL="${1:-https://comeals.com}" node tests/smoke/smoke.js
